# Future work — surfaces/blocks

- Nested reordering. The movable unit is a top-level block, so a writer cannot
  reorder one list item among its siblings from the handle. Rows and columns
  belong to the table surface (§4, deepest owner) and already have Alt+Arrows
  reserved for them; list items have no design yet. Whatever lands must keep
  the property that makes the current drop model safe: every seam resolves at a
  depth where the schema allows the moved node.

- Drag-scroll at the viewport edges. A drag that reaches the top or bottom of
  the scroll area currently stops there; a long manuscript wants the page to
  follow. Alt+↑/↓ is the keyboard answer meanwhile, and it scrolls the landing
  into view.

- Touch. §5.8 asks for a handle shown for the active block on tap, draggable.
  The pointer events here are pointer-type agnostic, so the missing piece is
  the reveal: a tap has no hover to settle.
